cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the Cart-State dataset, please cite the paper."
title: "Knowing vs. Saying: A Calibrated Dissociation Test for LLM Agents"
authors:
  - given-names: "Yugandhar Reddy"
    family-names: "Gogireddy"
    affiliation: "University of Southern California"
    email: "gogiredd@usc.edu"
date-released: "2026-06-24"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://anonymous.4open.science/r/dissociation-test"
abstract: >
  We introduce the dissociation test, a per-timestep diagnostic that
  decomposes LLM-agent failures into three mechanistically distinct
  failure modes (world-model, deployment, readout-bottleneck) via a
  signed gap between linear/MLP probe fidelity and behavioural
  accuracy, calibrated by a permutation null. Released artifacts:
  Cart-State (n=200 trajectories with exact ground truth), MiniGrid
  trajectories, hidden-state caches, probe weights, and intervention
  scripts.
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - interpretability
  - probing
  - mechanistic-interpretability
  - evaluation
  - world-model
  - dissociation
